Z||000000||dennis_6||10-14-2001||08:24 PM||||Is it poassible to put a long bed on a shortbed 1995 Silverado C1500?  Thanks!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierospeeder||10-15-2001||01:45 AM||||try going to the forum<BR> <A HREF="http://www.coloradok5.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.coloradok5.com</A>  <P>and ask those guys,  <BR>there more into the blazers but there is a truck section.  The blazers are almost identical to the trucks back in the 80s.<P>You can also try  <A HREF="http://www.plowsite.com" TARGET=_blank>www.plowsite.com</A>  and go to the chevy truck page.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||10-15-2001||03:58 AM||||My dad used to have a 88, which is the same body style. I don't think that the longer box will fit on it unless you lengthen the wheelbase. My dad put a 7 foot flatbed on his longbox and it required taking about 2 feet off of the frame (basically from right behind the rear leaf spring mount on back was removed) with the shortened frame on that it didn't look like a shortbed box would fit on it without the wheel well being  out of position.<p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 10-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||dennis_6||10-15-2001||04:59 AM||||Thanks for the information!||||reg||10
Z||000004||My7Fieros||10-15-2001||08:10 PM||||Just outta couriosity, why? More space or looks? Just wondering.||||reg||1
Z||000005||dennis_6||10-15-2001||11:52 PM||||Because it makes the truck bigger and that makes you a bigger man!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>But seriously my father was wanting a larger bed to carry stuff on.  In my family trucks are used as work vehicles, not as status symbols.<p>[This message has been edited by dennis_6 (edited 10-15-2001).]||||reg||1
